{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Glory over me — for when?</b> It refers back to: 'Glory over me — for when shall I send the children of Israel,' and I <b>will entreat for you</b> — that they be cut off immediately." "<b>And for your people.</b> The mem with sheva. Reason dictates that this plague did not last a quarter of the month, and if you say — it was the sixth day of the plague, and the plague lasted seven days; if so, why did Moses say to him <b>for when shall I entreat for you</b> — they are due to be cut off tomorrow!"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:31.034062574Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}